From 903a24bcca8be6d36af047d86d965b8539ae5e6b Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude Opus 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Mon, 14 Sep 2026 03:13:55 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Make the release-date column steer Wikipedia, socials and the
 game path

The year in the release-date column already decided which IMDb, Metacritic
and Rotten Tomatoes page a title got. It did not touch Wikipedia or the
Wikidata item -- and the Wikidata item is where the row's social handles
come from -- so a remake could ship the original's article and the
original's Instagram/X/Facebook. Video games ignored the date entirely.

Movies & TV:
* wiki_lookup ranks same-named articles by year (disambiguator first, then
  the item's own P577/P580) and reports whether the year could be confirmed.
* wikidata_meta prefers the item dated to the release year, and replaces a
  supplied qid that is the right kind but the wrong year.
* _enrich_by_tt takes the sheet's year rather than deriving it from
  released_on, which is blank for upcoming titles and often a festival date.
* The no-IMDb-id path now resolves a Wikipedia article at all.
* A curated Metacritic/RT URL carrying a different year no longer
  short-circuits the year-suffixed lookup.

Video games:
* fetch_game takes year_hint, so reboots resolve to the right item.
* A search hit whose name does not match is never used as the fallback.
* Wikipedia and IMDb fall back to a year-aware search when Wikidata has no
  sitelink and no P345 -- the common case for games.
* verify_socials is called with the title, and the band/VEVO guard no longer
  trips on publisher handles like bandainamco.

When the year cannot be confirmed the value is kept and flagged as a review
finding against its column; nothing is silently blanked.

